notes.body:
After some stumbling around, I came across this: 

```
if (ARES_IN_LOOPBACK(na) || /* 127.0.0.0/8 */
    (na & 0xffff0000) == 0xa9fe0000) /* 169.254.0.0/16 */
{
    return ARES_IPV6_ADDR_SCOPE_LINKLOCAL;
}
```

~~Didn't go further down in c-ares source code, but my guess is, they do not allow link-local lookups for security reasons. Have not found anything that would allow me to enable it. So sadly, that exact use case seems to be prevented.~~

